1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:01,280
Hi guys.

2
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:04,460
Today let's talk about communication in it.

3
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:10,670
Types of communication and practice present Continuous tense.

4
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:11,900
Let's go.

5
00:00:12,230 --> 00:00:12,830
Okay.

6
00:00:12,830 --> 00:00:19,700
People in it communicate mostly online and they use a lot of tools.

7
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:25,280
So people write emails using Outlook or Gmail.

8
00:00:25,310 --> 00:00:33,980
They post team notifications, project updates using Slack or Microsoft teams.

9
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:38,980
They might have video calls using Skype or Zoom.

10
00:00:38,990 --> 00:00:48,170
They might receive a message from recruiter or company or colleague in LinkedIn and they can post comments

11
00:00:48,170 --> 00:00:50,240
on code using Git.

12
00:00:50,270 --> 00:00:55,820
All right, let's have a look at some situations of company communication.

13
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:05,220
They are chatting near the water cooler, probably discussing something funny.

14
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:10,290
She is writing an email to her colleague.

15
00:01:12,590 --> 00:01:16,100
They are having a team meeting.

16
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:21,020
They are having a zoom.

17
00:01:21,870 --> 00:01:22,410
Call.

18
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:28,870
They are listening to the manager.

19
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:37,470
Okay for these sentences are used present continuous tense.

20
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:43,260
They are listening to the manager for this tense.

21
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:47,580
We take the verb to be in the right form.

22
00:01:47,730 --> 00:01:48,960
I am.

23
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:49,980
You are.

24
00:01:50,010 --> 00:01:51,150
They are.

25
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:52,500
He is.

26
00:01:52,620 --> 00:01:59,790
And we add ending inc to the main verb listening.

27
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:00,590
Okay.

28
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:07,710
We often use present continuous with words like now at the moment currently.

29
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:09,220
Okay.

30
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:13,090
Are they having a video call now?

31
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:15,610
No, they are not.

32
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:18,970
They are chatting near the cooler.

33
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:23,270
Is she writing an email?

34
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:25,580
Yes, she is.

35
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:28,520
Are they having?

36
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,700
Are they chatting near the cooler?

37
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:33,160
No, they are not.

38
00:02:35,150 --> 00:02:37,190
Are they having a zoom call?

39
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:40,070
No, they are not.

40
00:02:42,090 --> 00:02:44,490
Are they having a team meeting?

41
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:47,070
Yes, they are.

42
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:57,680
All right, let's have a look at these text messages and decide which message is notification in a team

43
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:06,230
channel request related to work, not business related message and job proposal.

44
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:11,150
Pause the video and look at these messages for a few seconds.

45
00:03:14,230 --> 00:03:15,270
All right.

46
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:16,170
Yes.

47
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:20,320
One is a business related message.

48
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:23,170
It's an email to a team member.

49
00:03:23,410 --> 00:03:26,590
Here we have informal greeting.

50
00:03:27,150 --> 00:03:30,600
Here we have a polite request.

51
00:03:30,630 --> 00:03:35,340
Could you please provide me the link to home page design?

52
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:39,780
So provide means send, share or give.

53
00:03:39,810 --> 00:03:42,360
Could you please send me the link?

54
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:45,540
And here we have a closing part.

55
00:03:45,570 --> 00:03:47,220
Best regards.

56
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:49,900
All right.

57
00:03:49,910 --> 00:03:53,960
These two messages are informal messages.

58
00:03:53,990 --> 00:03:58,950
First one is a notification in a team channel.

59
00:03:58,970 --> 00:04:01,580
Here we have informal greeting.

60
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:02,480
Hi, guys.

61
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:06,560
And then we have a short, informative message.

62
00:04:06,620 --> 00:04:08,640
I am not feeling very well.

63
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:12,380
I will take sick leave for today and probably tomorrow.

64
00:04:12,410 --> 00:04:14,510
The client is informed.

65
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:20,310
This one is a message to a friend or very close coworker.

66
00:04:20,330 --> 00:04:24,830
Here we don't have any greeting or closing parts.

67
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:28,040
I'm going downstairs to grab a cup of coffee.

68
00:04:28,070 --> 00:04:29,810
Do you want one?

69
00:04:30,110 --> 00:04:30,830
Okay.

70
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:36,210
This one is a job proposal.

71
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:38,740
Here we have informal greeting.

72
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:39,990
Hi, Katerina.

73
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:43,110
Then we have a proposal itself.

74
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:51,330
I'm currently looking to hire a freelance or part time HR and recruiter for our growing remote agency.

75
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:55,080
Currently means now at the moment.

76
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:57,120
And in this sentences.

77
00:04:57,970 --> 00:05:01,090
They used present continuous.

78
00:05:01,090 --> 00:05:04,540
